Cloud adoption should be measured using clearly defined technical and business metrics rather than assumptions.

Common success indicators include:

* Service availability
* Incident reduction
* Deployment speed
* Cost optimisation
* Customer satisfaction
* Compliance achievement
* Operational efficiency

For example, an organisation may compare application deployment times before and after migrating to Azure to evaluate operational improvements.

A real-life use case is executive leadership reviewing cloud performance dashboards to assess return on investment.

Measuring outcomes enables continuous improvement and informed decision-making.
